Theorem L-5: Finite lattice height

  Preconditions:
    - Each AimsState dimension has finite height per Annex E §AIMS.8 L-5
    - Per-dimension heights per Annex E §AIMS §3.1 through §AIMS §3.7:
        Access 1, Consumption 3, Cardinality 2, Uniqueness 2,
        Locality 4, Shape 1, Effect 3
    - height(L) for a chain of length k is k - 1 (height counts edges,
      not nodes); for a flat lattice with TOP it is 1; for a product
      lattice it is the sum of per-dimension heights

  Soundness property:
    height(AimsState) = sum of per-dimension heights
                     = 1 + 3 + 2 + 2 + 4 + 1 + 3
                     = 16
    No ascending chain in AimsState exceeds length 16.

  Proof obligation:
    Per-dimension finite-height witness via maximal-chain construction.

    Per-dimension maximal chains (length = chain edges = height):
      Access B < O (height 1)
      Consumption empty < L < A < U (height 3)
      Cardinality absent < 1 < omega (height 2)
      Uniqueness u < ms < s (height 2)
      Locality bl < fl < ae < he < top (height 4)
      Shape any_element < Phi (height 1)
                  (flat lattice; every non-Phi element has a single
                  upward edge to Phi; no chain of length > 1 exists
                  because non-Phi elements are mutually incomparable)
      Effect empty < {alloc} < {alloc, share}
                  < {alloc, share, throw} (height 3)
                  (one chain via the 3-bit flag inclusion order; total
                  height = 3 = number of flags)

    Each per-dimension carrier is FINITE by construction (explicit
    value enumeration in Annex E §AIMS.*); the carrier set
    is bounded and every chain is bounded by the maximal chain
    above. Therefore each dimension has finite height.

    Product height = sum of dimension heights:
      Standard product-lattice fact: for product L = L1 x L2 x ... x Ln
      with each Li a finite lattice, height(L) = sum_i height(Li).
      Construction witness: take the maximal chain in each dimension;
      lift it to the product by holding the other dimensions at their
      bottom element; concatenate per-dimension chains end-to-end
      after CN-canonicalization at each step. The resulting product
      chain has length 1 + 3 + 2 + 2 + 4 + 1 + 3 = 16.

    Matches Annex E §AIMS IA-7 CHAIN_HEIGHT = 16 (used as the
    intraprocedural convergence bound: CHAIN_HEIGHT * |variables| *
    |blocks|).

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (per-dimension height summation + chain construction
        per section_02::verify_l5_finite_height)
      monotonicity (validates the per-dimension order on which the
        chains are constructed is the same order L-6 covers)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: sec-02 lattice engine discharges L-5 via per-dimension chain enumeration + product sum to 16
